  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Provision of Movement Assistance in Camp As Sayliyah (CAS) Qatar</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">In August 2021, following the announcement of the withdrawal of the US and other international military forces from Afghanistan, the security situation in the country deteriorated at a fast pace, with a rapid advance of the Taliban and the eventual collapse of the Government on 15 August 2021. In this security context, most of the international actors present in Afghanistan evacuated embassy personnel, including local staff and Afghans who were current or former contractors and implementing partners for international actors. Through a large scale and time-sensitive logistical operation, thousands of Afghans were evacuated with their dependents. 
 
The overall goal of this project is to ensure the provision of safe and dignified movement assistance to all outbound travellers from Camp as Sayliyah (CAS). This can be furthered through consolidation of the outbound ticketing process at CAS under a single provider, streamlining and improving efficiency in ticketing operations. Beneficiaries of this project include Special Immigration Visa, refugees, and other migrants in Qatar.</narrative>
  </description>
